      "content": "i hear that, but it feels like the \"multifaceted\" answer is kind of avoiding the elephant in the room. when looking at modern social justice contexts, doesn't retributive justice actually lean into the same punitive systemic structures that these movements are trying to dismantle? it seems like restorative justice is the only one of the two that actually aligns with progress and human rights, whereas retributive justice just feels like an outdated way of maintaining control. don't you think it's more accurate to say one is progressive and the other is regressive?",
